{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1505858-how-does-the-realm-compare-to-older-edition-books","id":1505858,"title":"How does The Realm compare to older edition books.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-19T18:51:17-07:00","id":1505858,"title":"How does The Realm compare to older edition books.","content":"Hello! I am exploring Exalted Essence. It has reawakened my interest in Exalted. I have the 1st and 2nd edition books that dealt with the Blessed Isle. How does The Realm compare as a setting book, especially to the Terrestrial Directions one? Is it mostly a retread with a different writing style or does it bring a lot of newer materials? Thanks for any insight you can provide!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-19T21:33:48-07:00","id":1505880,"title":"","content":"I found it to be more than a re-treading, since the tone and scope of the game has shifted. I can't go too in-depth -it's been a bit since I read it- but the treatment gave a good update to setting information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T11:46:47-07:00","id":1506055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1505858-how-does-the-realm-compare-to-older-edition-books#post1505858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello! I am exploring Exalted Essence. It has reawakened my interest in Exalted. I have the 1st and 2nd edition books that dealt with the Blessed Isle. How does The Realm compare as a setting book, especially to the Terrestrial Directions one? Is it mostly a retread with a different writing style or does it bring a lot of newer materials? Thanks for any insight you can provide!</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty different. Basically it doesn't assume the 2e book at all, the timeline is updated (2e's was a copy-paste of 1e's), and and even geogrpahy. Like, some areas described as swamps in the 2e book are desert or arid in <i>The Realm</i>, and the home bases of different Great Housses is talked about a greater deal in 3e than in previous editions.<br /> <br /> There are also differences in governance, the Realm's caste system (including the definitions of things like patrician or Dyanst and the legal code), the miltiary, the Immaculate Philosophy, and how the Realm acquires and maintains satrapies. Some bits and bobs aesthetically like the Black Helms are talked about, but also given different context and details on how they operate. There's also a whole chapter on major satrapies in the Threshold, which serves as a role similar ot <i>Scavenger Sons</i> but for Realm-dominated locations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T18:16:21-07:00","id":1506100,"title":"","content":"It's also nice to not have random mention of &quot;half-Dragonblooded&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T00:25:49-07:00","id":1506124,"title":"","content":"I should note that <i>The Realm</i> is very much written as a complimentary book to 3e's <i>Dragon-Blooded: What Fire Has Wrought</i>. There's some bits in there that assume you know some of the details of WFHW, such as the different home bases of the Great Houses, Iselsi's current situation, and things like how many Dynastic and patrician households are structured. And WFHW also draws on things that the Realm talks about, such as the military structure, the way satrapies operate, and 3e's revised Realm timeline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T10:15:23-07:00","id":1506150,"title":"","content":"Things off the top of my head that The Realm does which set it apart from depictions of the Blessed Isle in prior Editions:<br /> <br /> History of the Realm itself has been overhauled to make it feel more dynamic; things like the origins of the Great Houses being pegged to particular times and given a sense of context and consequence, and a few more crises for it to face.<br /> <br /> Goes into more depth of the everyday culture of the Isle's inhabitants. Diversifies the landscape a lot and creates some different societies as a result of that. More description for the ethnic composition of the Isle, including the fact that it would be varied even before immigration during the Realm era.<br /> <br /> Imperial ministries are given more detail, with more emphasis on what their actual function in governing is rather than being a hotbed of murderous intrigue. A decent number of example ministries of varying importance are given.<br /> <br /> The All-Seeing Eye is overhauled significantly, going from &quot;basically House Iselsi who are now exposed to the disdain of the Great Houses in the exact same way the magistrates are&quot; to &quot;clandestine network with nobody at the top anymore, leaving them somewhere between struggling to define an agenda and having a lot of cells go rogue&quot;.<br /> <br /> Full dedicated chapters given for the Imperial military and the Immaculate Order; the former has a lot of familiar information gathered and streamlined and given a sense of how it translates practically to what they do day-to-day, the latter has some of the finer details of how the group is organized modified while going into more depth about their operations and motives.<br /> <br /> There's a large list of prefectures, that are each given a bit more depth and distinguishing characteristics. If it's the home of a Great House, you'll know fully what the House's impact on it has been. If it isn't, you'll probably know what value it could be for Houses to fight over controlling it in a civil war. Prefectures tend to have their own home-grown plot hooks, some of which are rather unconcerned with the larger context of the Realm.<br /> <br /> More thorough description of the manner in which the Realm has historically exerted influence abroad, including the processes and consequences for that authority breaking down. Several example satrapies of varying levels of independence. Also includes Prasad, the place that is de jure a satrapy but de facto a breakaway empire in its own right ruled by the descendants of Great Houses that went rogue.<br /> <br /> The most detailed description of the Caul, the great mysterious island that the Realm and Lunar Exalted war directly for control over.<br /> <br /> One important thing is that there's a greater sense of the scale of the Blessed Isle, including the fact that the Realm doesn't have absolute control over it. There's already room for things like bandit groups who can go a fair while before imperial troops could practically go after them, and mysterious wonders hidden away, as well as the remnants of cultures older than the Realm. That's important for making it a viable setting for Exalted other than Dragon-Blooded to function in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-21T15:02:58-07:00","id":1524374,"title":"","content":"This is really useful feedback. So far the 3e lore hasn't made me annoyed the same way 2e often copied and pasted stuff from 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}